s creates a new digit.\n\nSo the total would be 1 (billions) 4 (hundred millions) followed by the rest.\n\nSo the digits from left to right are:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo the number is 1,436,434,512?\n\nWait let me check step by step:\n\nStarting from the units:\n\nUnits digit: 0+2=2.\n\nTens:4+7=11. So 1 with carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:9+5=14 +1=15. 5, carryover1.\n\nThousands:9+1=10 +1=11. 1, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:2+0=2 +1=3.\n\nHundred thousands:5+9=14. 4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:1+1=2 +1=3.\n\nTen millions:3+3=6.\n\nHundred millions:6+8=14. 4 with carryover1.\n\nThen the billions place: the carryover1.\n\nSo the total number is 1 (billion), 4 (hundred million), then the rest of the digits:\n\nTen millions:6, Millions:3, hundred thousands:4, ten thousands:3, thousands:1, hundreds:5, tens:1, units:2.\n\nSo putting it together: 1,436,434,512?\n\nWait, but let me structure it properly:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:3?\n\nWait, no. Wait the breakdown:\n\nAfter adding:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nUnits:2\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:3\n\nTen millions:6\n\nHundred millions:4 (with carryover 1 to billions).\n\nWait the hundred millions digit was 6+8=14, so 4 with carryover 1 to the billions place. So the billions digit is 1, then the hundred millions is 4, ten millions 6, millions 3, etc.\n\nTherefore the number is written as 1,4 (hundred million), 6 (ten million), 3 (million), 4 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 1 (ten), 2 (unit).\n\nSo the number is 1,463,431,512?\n\nWait, let me write each part:\n\nBillions: 1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo the number is 1,463,431,512? Wait let me see:\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\n1 (billions)\n\n463,431,512\n\nWait, putting commas:\n\n1,463,431,512.\n\nWait, but let me check again step by step:\n\nStarting from the highest digit (billions):\n\nBillions:1\n\nThen hundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo combining them:\n\n1,463,431,512.\n\nYes. Let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n631,529,940\n\n+831,901,572\n\n= ?\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n631 million + 831 million = 1,462 million.\n\nThen the thousands:\n\n529 thousand + 901 thousand = 1,430 thousand.\n\nThen the units:\n\n940 + 572 = 1,512.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n1,462,000,000 + 1,430,000 = 1,463,430,000\n\nThen add 1,512:\n\n1,463,430,000 + 1,512 = 1,463,431,512.\n\nYes, that matches. So the sum is 1,463,431,512.\n\nTherefore the final answer is 1,463,431,512.\n</think>\n\nThe sum of 631,529,940 and 831,901,572 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n 631,529,940 \\\\\n+831,901,572 \\\\\n\\hline\n1,463,431,512 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Units Place:** \\(0 + 2 = 2\\)\n2. **Tens Place:** \\(4 + 7 = 11\\) (Write 1, carry over 1)\n3. **Hundreds Place:** \\(9 + 5 + 1 = 15\\) (Write 5, carry over 1)\n4. **Thousands Place:** \\(9 + 1 + 1 = 11\\) (Write 1, carry over 1)\n5. **Ten Thousands Place:** \\(2 + 0 + 1 = 3\\)\n6. **Hundred Thousands Place:** \\(5 + 9 = 14\\) (Write 4, carry over 1)\n7. **Millions Place:** \\(1 + 1 + 1 = 3\\)\n8. **Ten Millions Place:** \\(3 + 3 = 6\\)\n9. **Hundred Millions Place:** \\(6 + 8 = 14\\) (Write 4, carry over 1 to billions place)\n10. **Billions Place:** \\(0 + 0 + 1 = 1\\)\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{1463431512}\\)",
