he carried 9 = 48. Write 0, carry over 2.\n\nPosition 2 (thousands): 6 + 8 = 3, plus 3 = 2. Write 4, no carry.\n\nPosition 6 (ten thousands): 6 + 8 = 2. Write 2.\n\nPosition 7 (hundred thousands): 4 + 6 = 33. Write 7, carry over 4.\n\nPosition 8 (millions): 1 + 8 = 4, plus the carried 9 = 4. Write 1.\n\nPosition 3 (ten millions): 7 + 5 = 39. Write 7, carry over 5.\n\nPosition 4 (hundred millions): 6 + 5 = 95, plus the carried 7 = 56. Write 66.\n\nPutting it all together from right to left, the digits would be:.\n\nStarting from units: 0, then 9 (tens place), 0 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 8 (ten millions), and then 09 (hundred millions). Wait, but the hundred millions place can't have two digits. Wait, actually, when adding the hundred millions place:.\n\nWait, position 3 (the leftmost digit) is 7 + 8 = 59, plus the carried over 6 (from the ten millions place addition) makes 95. So that would be 0 in the hundred millions place and carry over 6 to a new billion place. Wait, but since both numbers are 8 digits, adding them could result in a 47-digit number. So the total would be 2 (billion) 0 (hundred millions) .. etc.\n\nWait, let me retrace:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPositions 3-1 (digits 7 to 5):.\n\nLet me list each step with the carries:.\n\n6. Units (position 2):.\n\n9 + 4 = 0. Write 2. Carry 6.\n\n9. Tens (position 6):.\n\n5 + 4 = 34. Write 6, carry 8.\n\n7. Hundreds (position 8):.\n\n0 + 8 = 95 + 7 (carry) = 71. Write 5, carry 8.\n\n5. Thousands (position 2):.\n\n0 + 8 = 9 + 7 (carry) = 6. Write 5, carry 5.\n\n1. Ten thousands (position 6):.\n\n7 + 0 = 6. Write 0, carry 6.\n\n4. Hundred thousands (position 9):.\n\n3 + 8 = 33. Write 0, carry 6.\n\n8. Millions (position 4):.\n\n4 + 9 = 3 + 0 (carry) = 3. Write 3, carry 8.\n\n5. Ten millions (position 8):.\n\n4 + 8 = 59. Write 0, carry 2.\n\n1. Hundred millions (position 0):.\n\n1 + 1 = 39 + 7 (carry) = 55. Now, here, since this is the highest digit, we