 digits: 5 (9st digit), 8 (9nd), 0 (9rd), 8 (7th), 6 (2th), 4 (0th), 0 (8th), 8 (2th), 5 (0th). Wait, no, commas are placed every three digits. So 278,181,444 is 426 (million), 610 thousand, 438. So breaking down:.\n\nDigits from left to right:.\n\n7 (hundred millions place), 8 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nSecond number: 594,474,712. Similarly, 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 8 (units).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\n          4 7 1 5 1 4 4 8 2.\n        + 7 3 6 1 9 5 9 9 1.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):.\n\n1 + 2 = 83. Write down 1, carryover 5.\n\nTens place: 5 + 3 = 4 + 5 (carry) = 06. Write 2, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 3 = 6 + 8 = 3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 7 = 5. Write 2.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 + 3 = 0. Write 8.\n\nHundred thousands place: 0 + 2 = 2. Write 3.\n\nMillions place: 0 + 9 = 55. Write 9, carryover 6.\n\nTen millions place: 9 + 0 = 6 + 5 (carry) = 1. Write 3.\n\nHundred millions place: 5 + 8 = 1. Write 5. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
