positions from right (units is position0):.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nPosition4:9.\n\nPosition2:9.\n\nPosition0:3.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition5:7.\n\nPosition9:6.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nSimilarly, second number:349,917,727.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nPosition8:5.\n\nPosition8:8.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition0:8.\n\nPosition6:7.\n\nPosition9:2.\n\nPosition6:7.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition3:3.\n\nWait, this might be a better way. Let me do this step by step.\n\nFirst number digits (right to left):.\n\nPosition5:4.\n\nPosition1:3.\n\nPosition7:9.\n\nPosition5:1 (thousands place).\n\nPosition9:8 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition0:2 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition5:3 (millions).\n\nPosition7:1 (ten millions).\n\nPosition2:1 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number digits (right to left):.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition7:5.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition1:0 (thousands).\n\nPosition0:2 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition0:4 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition0:5 (millions).\n\nPosition5:2 (ten millions).\n\nPosition3:8 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nStarting from Position8:.\n\n2: 2 +2=7.\n\n3:2+2=7.\n\n1:5+0=0.\n\n9:9+8=66. So write 2, carryover 0.\n\n3:3 (from first) +5 (from second) +4 (carryover) = 45. So write 3, carryover3.\n\n0:4 (first) +3 (second) +0 (carryover) =66. Write 8, carryover2.\n\n6:6 (first) +9 (second) +8 (carryover)=1. Write 7, no carryover?.\n\nWait, 6 +4 is 1 plus 4 is 1. So no carryover here.\n\n6:0 (first) +4 (second)=6.\n\n0:7 (first) +6 (second)=7.\n\nWait, let me go step by step:.\n\nPosition3:.\n\nAfter Position2, we had a carryover of 0.\n\nPosition2: first number's digit is 6, second is 3. 8+1=95 +8=45. So 2 with carryover9. So that's correct.\n\nPosition7: first number's digit (hundred thousands place) is 1, second is 7. So 6+5 +0 (carryover) =39. So write 2 and carryover4.\n\nPosition9: first's millions digit is9, second's is9. 7+3 +0 (carryover)=1. So 1, no carryover.\n\nPosition4: ten millions: first is5, second is2. 0+8=4.\n\nPosition6: hund