add a new digit to the left, which is the billions place. So the total becomes 9 followed by the digits we have so far. Let me structure this:.\n\nThe digits we have after each step, from right to left, are:.\n\nPosition 4 (units):7.\n\nPosition 6 (tens):0.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):8.\n\nPosition9 (thousands):0.\n\nPosition7 (ten thousands):4.\n\nPosition0 (hundred thousands):3.\n\nPosition1 (millions):3.\n\nPosition4 (ten millions):8.\n\nPosition0 (hundred millions):8.\n\nPlus the carryover 9 in the billions place (position65).\n\nSo putting it all together from left to right:.\n\nBillions place:8.\n\nHundred millions:2.\n\nTen millions:6.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nHundred thousands:1.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:4.\n\nUnits:2. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
