arryover now.\n\nPosition 3 (ten millions):4 +1=3, plus any carryover? Wait, the previous carryover was 6 which was added at position 6, so after that, there is no more carryover. So 9+0=4, write 2.\n\nPosition 5 (hundred millions):2 +5=5. Write down 4.\n\nPutting all the digits together from last to first (since we started from units):.\n\nThe digits we have written, from position 8 to 4 are:.\n\nPosition 3:1.\n\n4:1.\n\n8:7.\n\n7:3.\n\n4:9 (with a carryover).\n\n2:9 (with carryover 2).\n\nWait, actually, when writing the result, the digits should be in order from units to the highest place, so the total number would be:.\n\nStarting from Position 5 (hundred millions) down to Position 3 (units):.\n\nPosition 7:1.\n\nPosition2:0.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition8:2.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition1:1.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nSo putting them together: 3 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),6 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),3 (hundreds),5 (tens),4 (units). .\n\nWait, let me structure this properly. Let's see:.\n\nHundred millions place:1.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:2.\n\nUnits:8.\n\nSo the number is 525,910,158? Wait, let me check the places again. .\n\nWait, the positions after adding are:.\n\nPosition 3: 0 (hundred millions).\n\nPosition9:8 (ten millions).\n\nPosition0:0 (millions).\n\nPosition4:7 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition3:6 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition0:0 (thousands).\n\nPosition1:6 (hundreds).\n\nPosition3:4 (tens).\n\nPosition0:7 (units).\n\nSo combining them, it's 1 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 4 (tens), and 7 (units). .\n\nSo writing that out: 873,280,772. Hmm, but let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the addition steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers step by step more carefully. Let me write them vertically aligned:.\n\n       275,538,310.\n     +548,538,693.\n     -------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 3 +9 =1.\n\nTens: 3 +1=7.\n\nHundreds:0 +7=4.\n\nThousands:3 +3=7.\n\nTen thousands:4 +0=36 (write 9, carryover 2).\n\nHundred thousands:7 +1=46 +9 (carryover) =82 (write 8, carryover9).\n\nMillions:0 +9=2 +3=1 (carryover from previous).\n\nTen millions:6 +6=2 (no carryover since previous carryover was added to millions).\n\nHundred millions:0 +3=5. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
