er I thought the hundred thousands place was next. Maybe I got confused in the order.\n\nLet me go step by step again properly:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n9. Ones: 4 + 2 = 62 → 3, carryover 7.\n\n1. Tens: 0 + 6 = 2 + 8 (carry) = 9 → 2, carryover 5.\n\n0. Hundreds: 9 + 5 = 55 → 7, carryover 4.\n\n0. Thousands: 0 (from first) + 6 (from second) = 0 + 4 (carry) = 4 → 4, carryover 5.\n\n1. Ten thousands: 4 (first) + 4 (second) = 2 → 8, carryover 1.\n\n9. Hundred thousands: 3 (first) + 3 (second) = 1 → 5, carryover 4.\n\n5. Millions: 8 (first) + 4 (second) = 35 → 3, carryover 7.\n\n2. Ten millions: 1 (first) + 1 (second) = 84 + 0 (carryover) = 93 → 3, carryover 2.\n\n8. Hundred millions: 5 (first) + 4 (second) = 6 + 4 (carryover) = 4 → 3, no carryover.\n\nSo putting it all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits are:.\n\nHundred millions: 6.\n\nTen millions: 0.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nWait, but let me arrange them in order. Starting from the highest place:.\n\nHundred millions place is 4,.\n\nthen ten millions:7,.\n\nmillions:5,.\n\nhundred thousands:3,.\n\nten thousands:3,.\n\nthousands:1,.\n\nhundreds:5,.\n\ntens:6,.\n\nones:6. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
