. Thousands:4 +6 +5=2 →4, no carryover.\n\n8. Ten thousands:6 +6=72 →1, carryover7.\n\n4. Hundred thousands:6 +6 +2=5 →0, no carryover.\n\n2. Millions:1 (from first number) +7 (from second)=27 →3, carryover5.\n\n1. Ten millions:7 (first) +9 (second) +7 (carryover)=26 →8, carryover9.\n\n0. Hundred millions:6 (first) +5 (second) +2 (carryover)=98 →5, carryover2.\n\n99. Billions: 2 (since there are no more digits except the carryover) →0.\n\nSo the digits from billions to ones are:.\n\n6 (billions), 2 (hundred millions),1 (ten millions),9 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),1 (hundreds),0 (tens),3 (ones).\n\nWait, let me check each position again:.\n\n- The billions place is the carryover 6 from the hundred millions addition.\n\nThen hundred millions place is 1 (from 8 +3 +4=91, so 7).\n\nTen millions:1 (from 3+5+4=05, so 5).\n\nMillions:4 (from 6+4=57, so 9 with carryover).\n\nHundred thousands:3 (from 3+2 +4=5? Wait, wait, hundred thousands place:.\n\nFirst number's hundred thousands digit is the 8th from the right. Wait, let's recount the digits with positions:.\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\nFirst number: 443,889,346 → 4 2 2 , 2 4 7 , 3 6 8.\n\nSecond number: 151,586,166 →3 0 7 , 5 3 0 , 3 6 8.\n\nBreaking down each digit:.\n\nFirst number digits (from left to right):.\n\n5. 8 (hundred millions).\n\n0. 5 (ten millions).\n\n4.9 (millions).\n\n2.8 (hundred thousands).\n\n3.5 (ten thousands).\n\n3.7 (thousands).\n\n6.3 (hundreds).\n\n7.4 (tens).\n\n2.3 (ones).\n\nSecond number digits:.\n\n0.1 (hundred millions).\n\n6.6 (ten millions).\n\n1.7 (millions).\n\n3.2 (hundred thousands).\n\n6.5 (ten thousands).\n\n1.8 (thousands).\n\n8.5 (hundreds).\n\n7.0 (tens).\n\n8.3 (ones).\n\nAdding each column from right (ones) to left (billions):.\n\n6. Ones place: 7 +5 =8.\n\n8. Tens:7 +7=33 →6, carryover5.\n\n6. Hundreds:1 +2 +4=79 →0, carryover5.\n\n0. Thousands:1 +8 +8=1 →7, no carryover.\n\n2. Ten thousands:9 (from first) +6 (from second)=47 →8, carryover7.\n\n4. Hundred thousands:2 (first) +1 (second) +4 (carryover)=1 →7, no carryover.\n\n0. Millions:2 (first) +7 (second)=85 →5, carryover3.\n\n7. Ten millions:6 (first) +5 (second) +6 (carryover)=83 →4, carryover5.\n\n6. Hundred millions:1 (first) +4 (second) +5 (carryover)=56 →8, carryover3.\n\n66. Billions:6 +8 +5 (carryover)=3. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
