der. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nOnes place: 7 + 9 = 83 → 2, carryover 5.\n\nTens: 6 + 1 + 5 = 08 → 2, carryover 7.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 0 + 2 = 0 → 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 2 + 9 = 7 → 8.\n\nTen thousands: 2 + 2 = 7 → 4.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 6 = 41 → 6, carryover 3.\n\nMillions: 4 + 1 + 4 = 23 → 0, carryover 7.\n\nTen millions: 3 + 9 + 9 = 09 → 8, carryover 0.\n\nHundred millions: 9 + 7 + 4 = 6 → 3.\n\nWait, so the digits from right to left are:.\n\n9 (ones), 1 (tens), 1 (hundreds), 4 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 4 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions). So putting them in order from highest to lowest place:.\n\n6 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 4 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
