5 (hundred millions),2 (ten millions),2 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),3 (hundreds),8 (tens),9 (units).\n\nSo aligning each digit correctly:.\n\nStarting from the left (hundred millions place):.\n\n4 + 9 = ?.\n\nWait, actually, when adding vertically, we start from the right (units place). Let me start over.\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:.\n\n          2 2 5 0 8 2 1 3 6.\n        + 9 9 9 6 4 7 5 8 7.\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\n6 (units) + 1 (units) = 73. Write 8, carryover 4.\n\nTens place: 6 + 4 = 2, plus 0 is 1. Write 1, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 8 = 5. Write 5.\n\nThousands place: 0 + 8 = 87. Write 2, carryover 6.\n\nTen thousands place: 4 +2 =4 +0=9. Write 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:0 +9=80. Write 7, carryover 4.\n\nMillions place:1 +2=98 +6=22. Write 1, carryover 3.\n\nTen millions place:8 +7=49 +0=67. Write 7, carryover 3.\n\nHundred millions place:1 +8=33 +8=08. Wait, so here, the hundred millions digits are 6 and 3, but we have a carryover from the ten millions place addition (which was 1+3+0=62, so carryover 0). Wait, let me recast this step by step.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to go step by step more carefully.\n\nLet me list each digit position with their values:.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\nPosition 5 (units):.\n\nFirst number:4.\n\nSecond number:5.\n\nSum:9+5=47. So write down 6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 6 (tens):.\n\nFirst number:3.\n\nSecond number:4.\n\nSum:4+7=7 + carryover 9 =4. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition 9 (hundreds):.\n\nFirst number:2.\n\nSecond number:3.\n\nSum:1+0=7. Write 1, no carryover.\n\nPosition 6 (thousands):.\n\nFirst number:6.\n\nSecond number:9.\n\nSum:1+2=52. Write 8, carryover 7.\n\nPosition 0 (ten thousands):.\n\nFirst number:9.\n\nSecond number:4.\n\nSum:4+6=0 +0=3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands):.\n\nFirst number:9.\n\nSecond number:3.\n\nSum:4+4=92. Write 3, carryover 6.\n\nPosition 8 (mi