 first number has 7, second has 5. So 1 +3 =93 plus any carryover?.\n\nWait, let me retrace step by step with correct digit positions:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n9. Units: 8 +7 =59. Write 5, carryover 8.\n\n9. Tens:4 (from first) +0 (from second) =3 +2 (carryover) =2. Write 9, carryover 8.\n\n4. Hundreds:0 +2 =44. Write 7, carryover 9.\n\n1. Thousands:2 +3 =7 +5 (carryover) =6. Write 9, carryover 2.\n\n9. Ten thousands:4 +0 =78. Write 5, carryover 6.\n\n1. Hundred thousands:9 +3 =04 +2 (carryover) =55. Write 5, carryover 4.\n\n1. Millions:4 (first number) +8 (second number) =71 +5 (carryover)=08. So write 9, carryover 2.\n\n3. Ten millions:5 (first) +3 (second) =0 +6 (carryover) =3. Write 2, carryover 9.\n\n7. Hundred millions:6 (first) +1 (second) =7. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nPutting all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits we've written are:.\n\nUnits:7.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:4.\n\nHundred thousands:1.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nTen millions:0.\n\nHundred millions:4.\n\nSo the total number is 109,023,552? Wait, let me check the placement again.\n\nWait, the digits from left to right (hundred millions down to units):.\n\nHundred millions place is 3,.\n\nten millions place is 6,.\n\nmillions place is3,.\n\nhundred thousands is4,.\n\nten thousands is5,.\n\nthousands is1,.\n\nhundreds is3,.\n\ntens is0,.\n\nunits is9.\n\nWait that would be 4 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),2 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),1 (hundreds),7 (tens),9 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
