)\n   - **Hundred thousands place:** \\(4 + 8 = 12\\) (write 2, carry over 1)\n   - **Millions place:** \\(9 + 2 + 1 = 12\\) (write 2, carry over 1)\n   - **Ten millions place:** \\(4 + 9 + 1 = 14\\) (write 4, carry over 1)\n   - **Hundred millions place:** \\(6 + 7 + 1 = 14\\) (write 4, carry over 1)\n   - **Billions place:** \\(1\\) (carry over from the previous step)\n\n3. **Combining all the results from each place:**\n   - The digits from right to left are: 5 (ones), 5 (tens), 9 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 4 (ten millions), 4 (hundred millions), and 1 (billions).\n\nThus, the sum of 649,424,786 and 792,873,169 is \\(\\boxed{1442297955}\\).",
