      "index": 0,
      "text": "1,185, 438, 019. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carrying over. Maybe adding it another way?\n\nAlternatively, I can split the numbers into smaller parts. Let's see:\n\nFirst number: 193,045,295. Let's break it into millions, thousands, and units:\n193,045,295 = 100,000,000 + 93,000,000 + 45,000 + 295.\n\nSecond number: 582,363,719. Breaking down similarly:\n500,000,000 + 82,000,000 + 363,000 + 719.\n\nAdding the millions: 100,000,000 + 500,000,000 = 600,000,000.\n\nThen the next parts: 93,000,000 + 82,000,000 = 175,000,000.\n\nNext, 45,000 + 363,000 = 408,000.\n\nFinally, 295 + 719 = 1,014.\n\nNow adding all those together: 600,000,000 + 175,000,000 = 775,000,000.\n\n775,000,000 + 408,000 = 775,408,000.\n\n775,408,000 + 1,014 = 775,409,014.\n\nWait a minute, that's different from my first result. Hmm, so I must have messed up the first method. Let me try adding again step by step.\n\nLet me write them out without commas for clarity:\n\n193045295\n\n+582363719\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 5 + 9 = 14. Write down 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 9 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 7 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 3 + 1 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 4. Write 4.\n\nMillions place: 3 + 2 = 5. Write 5.\n\nTen-millions place: 9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-millions place: 1 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 7.\n\nPutting it all together: 7 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions?), wait let me check the positions again.\n\nWait maybe I messed up the digit positions. Let's align them properly:\n\nLet me write each number with commas to see:\n\nFirst number: 193,045,295\n\nSecond number: 582,363,719\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nDigit 1 (units): 5 + 9 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nDigit 2 (tens): 9 + 1 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nDigit 3 (hundreds): 2 + 7 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nDigit 4 (thousands): 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0\n\nDigit 5 (ten thousands): 4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands): 0 + 3 = 3 + 1 (carry) = 4 \u2192 4, carry 0\n\nDigit 7 (millions): 3 + 2 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0\n\nDigit 8 (ten millions): 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nDigit 9 (hundred millions): 1 + 5 = 6 + 1 (carry) = 7 \u2192 7\n\nPutting all digits together from right to left: 7 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (units).\n\nWait, but writing that out: 7 (hundred millions), then 7, 5, 4, 0, 9, 0, 1, 4.\n\nWait, so the number is 775,049,014? But when I broke it down earlier, I got 775,409,014. Hmm, discrepancy between the two methods. Which is correct?\n\nWait let's do the breakdown again:\n\nFirst number: 193,045,295\n\nBreaking down:\n\n100,000,000 + 90,000,000 + 3,000,000 + 40,000 + 5,000 + 200 + 90 +5\n\nSecond number:582,363,719\n\n500,000,000 +80,000,000 +2,000,000 +300,000 +60,000 +3,000 +700 +10 +9\n\nAdding each part:\n\nHundred millions: 100M +500M =600M\n\nTens of millions: 90M +80M=170M\n\nMillions: 3M +2M=5M \u2192 total so far: 600+170+5=775M\n\nHundred thousands: 0 +300,000=300k\n\nTen thousands:40k +60k=100k \u2192 total: 300k+100k=400k\n\nThousands:5k +3k=8k \u2192 total:400k+8k=408k\n\nHundreds:200+700=900\n\nTens:90+10=100 \u2192 100+900=1,000\n\nUnits:5+9=14 \u2192 total units:14 \u2192 so 1,000+14=1,014\n\nNow, adding all these:\n\n775,000,000 +408,000=775,408,000\n\nThen add 1,014: 775,408,000 +1,014=775,409,014.\n\nBut when I did the digit-by-digit addition earlier, I ended up with 775,049,014. So which is correct?\n\nAh! I think I messed up the digit-by-digit positions. Let me check again:\n\nLet me write the numbers with their digits separated:\n\nFirst number: 1 9 3 0 4 5 2 9 5\n\nSecond number:5 8 2 3 6 3 7 1 9\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nDigit 1:5 (first) +9 (second)=14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nDigit 2:9 +1=10 +1 (carry)=11\u21921, carry1\n\nDigit3:2 +7=9 +1=10\u21920, carry1\n\nDigit4:5 +3=8 +1=9\u21929, carry0\n\nDigit5:4 +6=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit6:0 +3=3 +1=4 \u21924, carry0\n\nDigit7:3 +2=5 \u21925\n\nDigit8:9 +8=17 \u21927, carry1\n\nDigit9:1 +5=6 +1=7\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n4 (units),1 (tens),0 (hundreds),9 (thousands),0 (ten thousands),4 (hundred thousands),5 (millions),7 (ten millions),7 (hundred millions)\n\nSo constructing the number: 7 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),5 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),0 (hundreds),1 (tens),4 (units).\n\nWait, so that would be 775,049,014. But the other method gave 775,409,014. The difference is in the hundred thousands and ten thousands places. Hmm, so where is the mistake?\n\nWait when breaking down the numbers:\n\nFirst number's ten thousands place: 4 (from 193,045,295: the '04' in the middle is the ten thousands place? Wait let me parse 193,045,295 properly.\n\nBreaking down 193,045,295:\n\nBillions: 0\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:5\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:9\n\nUnits:5\n\nWait, actually, commas are placed every three digits starting from the right. So 193,045,295 is:\n\n1 (hundred million), 9 (ten million), 3 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 9 (ten), 5 (unit).\n\nSimilarly, 582,363,719 is:\n\n5 (hundred million),8 (ten million),2 (million),3 (hundred thousand),6 (ten thousand),3 (thousand),7 (hundred),1 (ten),9 (unit).\n\nTherefore, adding the ten thousands place:\n\nFirst number has 4 (ten thousands), second has 6 (ten thousands). 4 +6=10. So that's 0 with a carryover of 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: first number has 0, second has 3. Plus the carried 1 makes 4. So that's correct. So in the digit-by-digit addition, the ten thousands digit is 0 (from 4+6=10), and the hundred thousands is 4 (0+3+1). So the hundred thousands place is the 4, and the ten thousands is 0.\n\nTherefore, the digit-by-digit total is 775,049,014.\n\nBut when I broke down the numbers, I think I miscalculated the breakdown. Let me check again:\n\nBreaking into parts:\n\nFirst number: 100,000,000 (hundred million) + 90,000,000 (ten million) + 3,000,000 (million) + 0 (hundred thousand) + 40,000 (ten thousand) +5,000 (thousand) + 200 (hundred) +90 (ten) +5 (unit).\n\nSecond number: 500,000,000 (hundred million) +80,000,000 (ten million) +2,000,000 (million)+300,000 (hundred thousand)+60,000 (ten thousand)+3,000 (thousand)+700 (hundred)+10 (ten)+9 (unit).\n\nAdding the hundred thousands:\n\nFirst number has 0, second has 300,000 \u2192 total 300,000.\n\nTen thousands: first has 40,000, second has 60,000 \u2192 total 100,000. So total for those two places: 300k +100k=400k. Then thousands: 5k +3k=8k. So adding to the millions:\n\nMillions place: 3,000,000 +2,000,000=5,000,000.\n\nSo combining all:\n\nHundred millions: 100M +500M=600M\n\nTen millions:90M +80M=170M\n\nMillions:3M +2M=5M \u2192 total so far is 600+170+5=775,000,000\n\nThen the hundred thousands and below:\n\nHundred thousands: 0+300k=300k\n\nTen thousands:40k+60k=100k \u2192 total 400k\n\nThousands:5k+3k=8k \u2192 total 408k\n\nAdding 408k to the 775,000,000 gives 775,408,000.\n\nThen the hundreds, tens, units:\n\n200+700=900\n\n90+10=100 \u2192 total 1,000\n\n5+9=14 \u2192 total 1,014.\n\nAdding 1,014 to 775,408,000 gives 775,409,014. Wait, but according to the digit-by-digit, it's 775,049,014. There's a discrepancy of 360,000. So where did I go wrong?\n\nAh! Wait, when adding the hundred thousands and ten thousands, in the breakdown method, I considered hundred thousands as 300k and ten thousands as 100k, so total 400k. But in digit-by-digit, the hundred thousands place ended up as 4 (from 0 +3 +1), and the ten thousands as 0 (from 4+6 +0). So the total from hundred thousands down would be 400,000 (hundred thousands place 4 is 400k) plus 0 ten thousands, but in the breakdown, it's 400k (300+100). Wait, maybe in the breakdown, I added the ten thousands (40k +60k=100k), so that's 100k, which is ten thousands place being 0 and hundred thousands place being 1? Wait no, ten thousands is a separate place.\n\nWait perhaps my breakdown is wrong. Let me think:\n\nWait, the hundred thousands place is the 6th digit from the right. Let me count:\n\nNumber: 775,049,014.\n\nBreaking down:\n\nDigit 1 (units):4\n\nDigit2:1\n\nDigit3:0\n\nDigit4:9 (thousands)\n\nDigit5:4 (ten thousands?) Wait no:\n\nWait commas are placed as hundred millions, ten millions, millions, then hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, etc.\n\nWait 775,049,014 is structured as:\n\n7 (hundred millions),\n\n7 (ten millions),\n\n5 (millions),\n\n0 (hundred thousands),\n\n4 (ten thousands),\n\n9 (thousands),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n4 (units).\n\nAh, so the hundred thousands digit is 0, the ten thousands is 4. In the breakdown method, the ten thousands place had 40k +60k=100k, so the ten thousands digit should be 0 with a carryover to the hundred thousands. But in the breakdown, I added the hundred thousands (0 +300k) and ten thousands (40k+60k=100k), so total of 400k, but in reality, the ten thousands place can only hold up to 99,999, so the 100k would carryover to hundred thousands.\n\nWait, breaking down:\n\nThe hundred thousands place is 0 (from first number) +300,000 (second number) plus any carryover from the ten thousands place.\n\nThe ten thousands place is 40,000 (first) +60,000 (second) =100,000. So this is 100,000, which is 1*100,000, so that would contribute 1 to the hundred thousands place. So the ten thousands digit becomes 0, and the hundred thousands becomes 0 +300k +100k's carryover (100k is 1*100k, so carryover 1 to hundred thousands). So hundred thousands becomes 300k +100k? Wait no, 300k is already in the second number's hundred thousands place. Wait I'm getting confused.\n\nLet me think of it as:\n\nTotal ten thousands: 40k +60k =100k. This is 1*100,000, so the ten thousands digit is 0 and we carry 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nTotal hundred thousands: 0 (from first) +300k (second) +1 (carry) = 301,000? Wait no, no, the carryover is 1 to the hundred thousands place, so the hundred thousands becomes 0 +300,000 +1*100,000? Wait no, the hundred thousands place is 0 +300,000, plus the carryover from ten thousands (which is 1). So the total in hundred thousands place is 300,000 +100,000 (carryover from ten thousands)? Wait no, the carryover is 1, representing 1*100,000, so adding to the hundred thousands:\n\nHundred thousands: 0 (first) +300,000 (second) +1*100,000 (carryover) = 400,000. Therefore, the hundred thousands digit is 4 (400,000) and the ten thousands is 0. So that matches the digit-by-digit result where hundred thousands is 4 and ten thousands is 0. Therefore, the total from those places is 400,000. So adding to the millions: 5,000,000 +400,000 =5,400,000. Then adding to the hundred millions total (775,000,000):\n\nWait no, let me recast the breakdown:\n\nTotal hundred millions and above:\n\n700,000,000 (from 100M+500M) + 170,000,000 (ten millions) +5,000,000 (millions) = 700+170=870 +5=875? Wait wait, that contradicts previous.\n\nWait my breakdown earlier had:\n\nHundred millions: 100M +500M =600M\n\nTen millions:90M +80M=170M\n\nMillions:3M +2M=5M\n\nSo total up to millions:600+170+5=775,000,000.\n\nThen the hundred thousands place after adding carryover is 400,000 (from 0+300k +100k carryover). Ten thousands is 0, thousands is 8k, etc. So the next part after 775,000,000 is adding 400,000 (hundred thousands) + 0 (ten thousands) +8,000 (thousands) =408,000.\n\nThen adding the hundreds, tens, units:1,014. So total is 775,000,000 +408,000 =775,408,000 +1,014 =775,409,014. Wait but according to digit-by-digit, it's 775,049,014. Hmm, there must be an error here.\n\nWait, perhaps in the breakdown I miscalculated the hundreds, tens, units?\n\nFirst number's hundreds:200, tens:90, units:5\n\nSecond number's hundreds:700, tens:10, units:9\n\nAdding those:\n\nHundreds:200 +700=900\n\nTens:90+10=100 \u2192 which is 100 + 900 = 1,000\n\nUnits:5+9=14 \u2192 total 1,000 +14=1,014. That seems right.\n\nSo where is the discrepancy?\n\nWait, in the digit-by-digit addition, the digits are:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 (units),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n9 (thousands),\n\n0 (ten thousands),\n\n4 (hundred thousands),\n\n5 (millions),\n\n7 (ten millions),\n\n7 (hundred millions).\n\nSo the number is 7 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),5 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),0 (hundreds),1 (tens),4 (units) \u2192 775,049,014.\n\nBut in the breakdown method, I have 775,409,014. The difference is in the millions place. Wait in digit-by-digit, the millions digit is 5, but in breakdown, I have 5,000,000 as part of the millions. Let me see:\n\nIn digit-by-digit, the millions place (digit 7 from the right):\n\nFirst number's millions digit is 3 (from 193,045,295: the millions digit is the 3 in 193), and second number's millions digit is 2 (from 582, so 2 in 582). So 3 +2 =5, which matches. So millions place is indeed 5.\n\nThen ten millions place: first number's ten millions digit is 9 (from 193), second number's is 8 (from 582). 9+8=17, so 7 with a carryover 1. That gives the ten millions digit as 7, and carryover to hundred millions. Hundred millions digits are 1+5=6 plus the carryover 1 makes 7. So that's correct.\n\nSo the digit-by-digit result is 775,049,014, whereas the breakdown method gave me 775,409,014. The difference is in the hundred thousands and ten thousands places.\n\nWait in the digit-by-digit, the hundred thousands digit is 4, ten thousands is 0. In the breakdown, I thought that the hundred thousands should be 400,000, which would be digit 4 in hundred thousands place. So that matches. The ten thousands digit is 0, so that's also correct. So the total from those places is 400,000 +0 =400,000. Then adding that to the millions:\n\nWait the millions part was 5,000,000 (from 3+2) plus the 400,000? Wait no, the millions are 5,000,000. The hundred thousands is a separate place. So the total up to millions is 775,000,000 (from 600+170+5). Then adding hundred thousands (400k), ten thousands (0), thousands (8k), etc. So 775,000,000 +408,000 (from 400k+8k) = 775,408,000. Then add the 1,014 \u2192775,409,014.\n\nWait but digit-by-digit gives 775,049,014. This inconsistency must be due to a miscalculation somewhere. Wait maybe in the breakdown, I added the ten thousands and hundred thousands incorrectly.\n\nWait let's do the breakdown again carefully:\n\nFirst number: 193,045,295.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n100,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n90,000,000 (ten million)\n\n3,000,000 (million)\n\n0 (hundred thousand)\n\n40,000 (ten thousand)\n\n5,000 (thousand)\n\n200 (hundred)\n\n90 (ten)\n\n5 (unit).\n\nSecond number:582,363,719.\n\n500,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n80,000,000 (ten million)\n\n2,000,000 (million)\n\n300,000 (hundred thousand)\n\n60,000 (ten thousand)\n\n3,000 (thousand)\n\n700 (hundred)\n\n10 (ten)\n\n9 (unit).\n\nAdding each corresponding part:\n\nHundred millions:100M +500M =600M\n\nTen millions:90M +80M =170M\n\nMillions:3M +2M =5M \u2192 total so far: 600+170+5 =775,000,000.\n\nHundred thousands:0 +300,000 =300,000\n\nTen thousands:40k +60k =100k \u2192 which is 100,000. So this 100k would add to the hundred thousands place.\n\nWait here's the mistake! The ten thousands place is 40k +60k =100k. That 100k is equivalent to 1 hundred thousand, so you have to carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place. So the ten thousands digit becomes 0, and the hundred thousands becomes 300k +100k (from the carryover) =400k. So the hundred thousands digit is 4 (400k) and the ten thousands is 0. So the total for hundred thousands and below up to million:\n\nHundred thousands:400,000\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nThousands:5k +3k =8k \u2192 8,000\n\nHundreds:200+700=900\n\nTens:90+10=100 \u2192 which is 100 +900 =1,000\n\nUnits:5+9=14 \u2192 total 1,014.\n\nSo adding all after 775M:\n\n400,000 +0 +8,000 =408,000\n\nAdding 408,000 to 775,000,000 gives 775,408,000.\n\nThen add the 1,014: 775,408,000 +1,014 =775,409,014.\n\nBut in the digit-by-digit, it's 775,049,014. So there's a discrepancy of 360,000. Where is this coming from?\n\nWait in digit-by-digit, the total after hundred thousands is 400,000 (hundred thousands) but in the digit-by-digit breakdown, the ten thousands digit is 0 and the hundred thousands is 4, so that's correct. Then the thousands digit is 9, which is 9,000. Wait, in digit-by-digit, thousands place was 5 +3 + carryover?\n\nWait let's re-examine the digit-by-digit step-by-step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nDigit 1 (units):5+9=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nDigit2 (tens):9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):2+7=9 +1=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit4 (thousands):5 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carry)=9 \u21929, carry0\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):4 (first) +6 (second)=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):0 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carry)=4 \u21924, carry0\n\nDigit7 (millions):3 +2=5 \u21925\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):9 +8=17 \u21927, carry1\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):1+5+1=7.\n\nSo the thousands digit is indeed 9 (i.e., 9,000), so total for thousands is 9,000. But in the breakdown, we had 5k +3k=8k. Wait why the difference?\n\nAh! Here's the mistake. In the breakdown, I said first number's thousands digit is 5,000 and second's is 3,000, totaling 8,000. But in digit-by-digit, the thousands digit (5+3)=8, plus carryover? Wait in digit4 (thousands place):\n\nFirst number's thousands digit is 5 (from 193,045,295: the '5' in the thousands place?), let's confirm:\n\nNumber:193,045,295.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n1 (hundred million),9 (ten million),3 (million),0 (hundred thousand),4 (ten thousand),5 (thousand),2 (hundred),9 (ten),5 (unit). So yes, thousands digit is 5.\n\nSecond number:582,363,719.\n\n5 (hundred million),8 (ten million),2 (million),3 (hundred thousand),6 (ten thousand),3 (thousand),7 (hundred),1 (ten),9 (unit). So thousands digit is 3.\n\nSo adding 5 +3 gives 8, but in digit4 (thousands place), we have 5 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carry from hundreds place) =9. Wait why is there a carryover?\n\nWait the hundreds place (digit3) had a carryover of 1. Let me retrace:\n\nDigit3 (hundreds place):\n\nFirst number:2, second:7 \u21922+7=9 +1 (carry from tens) =10 \u21920 with carry1 to thousands place.\n\nSo thousands place:5+3 +1 (carry) =9. So thousands digit is 9, so that's 9,000. But in my breakdown, I added 5k +3k=8k. This is the mistake! The thousands place has an extra 1k from the carryover. Therefore, the thousands are actually 9,000 instead of 8,000. That explains the discrepancy.\n\nTherefore, in the breakdown method, I forgot to account for the carryover from the hundreds place into the thousands. So the correct thousands total is 9,000, not 8,000. Therefore:\n\nContinuing the breakdown correctly:\n\nThousands place:9,000 (due to carryover), so adding:\n\nAfter hundred thousands:\n\n400,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n9,000 (thousands)\n\nHundreds:900\n\nTens and units:1,014.\n\nSo total after millions:\n\n400,000 +0 +9,000 =409,000.\n\nAdding to 775,000,000: 775,000,000 +409,000 =775,409,000.\n\nThen adding hundreds, tens, units:900 +1,014=1,914 \u2192 total becomes 775,409,000 +1,914=775,410,914? Wait no, perhaps I'm confused.\n\nWait let me recalculate:\n\nAfter 775,000,000 (hundred millions, ten millions, millions):\n\nThen adding the hundred thousands down:\n\n400,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n9,000 (thousands)\n\nSo 400k +0 +9k =409,000.\n\nAdding to 775,000,000 gives 775,409,000.\n\nThen the hundreds place:200+700=900 \u2192 so 900.\n\nTens and units: the tens were 90+10=100 and units 14, totaling 1,014. So 900 +1,014=1,914.\n\nAdding to 775,409,000: 775,409,000 +1,914 =775,410,914? Wait but this still doesn't align with the digit-by-digit total.\n\nWait perhaps I need to think in total:\n\nThe total from digit-by-digit is 775,049,014.\n\nWait let's compute both numbers with the correct thousands:\n\nFirst number:193,045,295\n\nSecond number:582,363,719\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me use another method: adding the numbers step by step.\n\n193,045,295\n\n+582,363,719\n\n-------------\n\nStart with the units:\n\n5+9=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nTens:9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nHundreds:2+7=9 +1=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nThousands:5+3=8 +1=9 \u21929, carry0\n\nTen thousands:4+6=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nHundred thousands:0+3=3 +1=4 \u21924, carry0\n\nMillions:3+2=5 \u21925\n\nTen millions:9+8=17 \u21927, carry1\n\nHundred millions:1+5=6 +1=7.\n\nSo the result is 775,049,014. Therefore, the correct total is 775,049,014.\n\nThe mistake in the breakdown was in the thousands place where I forgot the carryover from the hundreds place. So the thousands are 9,000, but then adding the hundreds (900), tens (100), units (14) gives:\n\n9,000 +900 =9,900; 9,900 +100 =10,000; 10,000 +14=10,014.\n\nSo adding that to the previous total:\n\n775,000,000 (millions and above) +400,000 (hundred thousands) +10,014 (the rest) \u2192 775,000,000 +410,014 =775,410,014? Wait no, let's see:\n\nWait, the breakdown should be:\n\nAfter millions:\n\nHundred thousands:400,000\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nThousands:9,000\n\nTotal up to thousands:409,000\n\nThen hundreds, tens, units:900 +100 +14 =1,014. So total from those is 409,000 +1,014 =410,014.\n\nAdding to 775,000,000 \u2192 775,000,000 +410,014 =775,410,014. But this still doesn't match the digit-by-digit result of 775,049,014.\n\nWait now I'm really confused. There must be a miscalculation here. Let me try adding the two numbers numerically without any breakdown:\n\nFirst number: 193,045,295\n\nSecond number:582,363,719\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n5 +9 =14 \u21