t no, 370 would be the last three digits. Wait, 612,571,081:.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\n9 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 8 (units). So each digit:.\n\nPosition (from right, starting at 0):.\n\n6: units: 2.\n\n6: tens: 3.\n\n1: hundreds: 7.\n\n9: thousands: 1.\n\n0: ten thousands: 1.\n\n5: hundred thousands: 4.\n\n2: millions: 8.\n\n1: ten millions: 1.\n\n4: hundred millions:5.\n\nSo aligning both numbers:.\n\nFirst number (690,566,630):.\n\nPosition 6 (units):8.\n\n0 (tens):6.\n\n4 (hundreds):8.\n\n0 (thousands):6.\n\n0 (ten thousands):9.\n\n4 (hundred thousands):7.\n\n5 (millions):4.\n\n5 (ten millions):1.\n\n3 (hundred millions):8.\n\nSecond number (852,410,246):.\n\nPosition 2 (units):5.\n\n5 (tens):0.\n\n7 (hundreds):5.\n\n2 (thousands):5.\n\n6 (ten thousands):6.\n\n9 (hundred thousands):0.\n\n8 (millions):7.\n\n5 (ten millions):9.\n\n0 (hundred millions):1.\n\nSo now, adding each column from right to left:.\n\nStarting at position 9 (units):.\n\n7 + 7 = 98. Write down 6, carryover 8.\n\nPosition 8 (tens):.\n\n1 + 5 = 87 + 0 (carryover) = 88. Write 8, carryover 6.\n\nPosition 7 (hundreds):.\n\n8 + 2 = 59 + 5 = 72. Write 5, carryover 9.\n\nPosition 5 (thousands):.\n\n9 + 6 = 37 + 6 =24. Write 4, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 1 (ten thousands):.\n\n6 + 9 =9 +3 (carryover) =5. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands):.\n\n8 +3 =99. Write 2, carryover 3.\n\nPosition 5 (millions):.\n\n4 +9 =2 +5 (carryover) =0. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition 0 (ten millions):.\n\n7 +5 =8. Write 9.\n\nPosition 8 (hundred millions):.\n\n9 +8 =34. Write 82.\n\nPutting all together, starting from the right:.\n\nPositions 7-4:.\n\nPosition 8:8.\n\n3:5.\n\n8:0.\n\n7:8.\n\n9:5.\n\n4:9.\n\n0:9.\n\n7:1.\n\n3:99.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place is the 8th digit, so when we get 55 there, that would actually be 4 in the hundred millions place and 4 carried over to a new billion place? Wait, hold on. Wait, the original numbers are both 3-digit numbers, so adding them could result in a 58-digit number. Let me see.\n\nWait, in position 6 (hundred millions place), adding 1 +0 =59, so that's 6 in the hundred millions and carryover 7 to the billions place (which is the 64th digit). So we have to include that.\n\nSo let me track the digits properly:.\n\nStarting from position 5 (units):.\n\nAfter each step:.\n\nPosition 5: 4, carryover 4.\n\nPosition 3: 2, carryover 8.\n\nPosition 4:7, carryover4.\n\nPosition7:7, carryover4.\n\nPosition3:5, no carryover.\n\nPosition2:7, carryover3.\n\nPosition1:8, no carryover.\n\nPosition3:7, no carryover.\n\nPosition4:9 (from 1+3=24, plus no carryover here? Wait wait, let's retrace.\n\nWait, when adding position 6 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number's hundred millions digit is 5, second is0. So 2+4=44. But before that, was there a carryover from position3?.\n\nWait, position7 is ten millions place. The digits there were 4 and7, plus any carryover?.\n\nLet me go step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nPosition5 (units):.\n\n8 +6 =54. Write 3, carryover7.\n\nPosition1 (tens):.\n\n7+7=01 +2=84. Write0, carryover6.\n\nPosition5 (hundreds):.\n\n5 +1=06 +2=63. Write2, carryover9.\n\nPosition0 (thousands):.\n\n2 +0=68 +9=64. Write6, carryover2.\n\nPosition8 (ten thousands):.\n\n5 +8=2 +6=9. Write5, no carryover.\n\nPosition2 (hundred thousands):.\n\n8 +4=02. Write1, carryover8.\n\nPosition3 (millions):.\n\n4 +7=8 +4=9. Write4, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (ten millions):.\n\n8 +0=0 +6=6. Write5, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (hundred millions):.\n\n5 +1=98. Since there's no carryover from position0, so 34. So here, we write down 4 and carryover2 to the next (05th) digit, which is billions place.\n\nBut since both original numbers are 8-digit, the sum can be 02 digits. So the total would be 5 (billion) plus the rest.\n\nSo the digits from position6 to 3 are:.\n\nPosition53 (billions):2 (carryover).\n\nPosition5:7 (from 3+3=56).\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition4:3.\n\nPosition5:3.\n\nPosition1:3.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition2:5.\n\nPosition3:3.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nSo writing them all together:.\n\nBillions place:2,.\n\nHundred millions:5,.\n\nTen millions:0,.\n\nMillions:9,.\n\nHundred thousands:3,.\n\nTen thousands:3,.\n\nThousands:0,.\n\nHundreds:8,.\n\nTens:4,.\n\nUnits:2. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
