rry1\n\n1 (hundred thousands) +0 (hundred thousands)=1 +1=2 \u21922, no carry\n\n5 (millions) +3 (millions)=8 \u21928\n\n0 (ten millions) +7 (ten millions)=7\n\n4 (hundred millions) +7 (hundred millions)=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nThe carryover 1 goes to billions place, making it 1.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1,136,023,660? Wait, let me write the digits:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:1 (from 4+7=11, so first digit after carry is 1)\n\nTen millions:3 (Wait no, the ten millions digit was 0+7=7, but with carryover? Wait:\n\nWait, let me structure the digits properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, the digits of the sum are:\n\nUnits:0\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nMillions:8\n\nTen millions:7\n\nHundred millions:1 (from 4+7=11)\n\nBillions:1 (carryover)\n\nSo the number is:\n\nBillions place:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:7,\n\nMillions:8,\n\nHundred thousands:2,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:4,\n\nHundreds:7,\n\nTens:6,\n\nUnits:0.\n\nWait, that would be 1,178,240,760.\n\nWait, let me separate each digit:\n\nPosition (from right, 1-based):\n\nPosition 1: 0 (units)\n\nPosition 2:6 (tens)\n\nPosition3:7 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:4 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:0 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition6:2 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition7:8 (millions)\n\nPosition8:7 (ten millions)\n\nPosition9:1 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition10:1 (billions)\n\nThus the number is 1,178,240,760.\n\nWait, let me test with calculator approach:\n\n405,113,796 +730,909,864 =\n\nLet me compute 405 million +730 million = 1,135 million.\n\nThen 113 thousand + 909 thousand = 1,022 thousand.\n\nThen 796 +864 = 1,660.\n\nAdding all together: 1,135,000,000 + 1,022,000 = 1,136,022,000 + 1,660 = 1,136,023,660.\n\nWait, so discrepancy here. Earlier step-by-step gave 1,136,023,660 but my digit-by-digit had a different number.\n\nHmm, where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, let's redo the digit-by-digit carefully:\n\nNumbers:\n\n405,113,796\n\n730,909,864\n\nAligning them:\n\n4 0 5 1 1 3 7 9 6\n\n7 3 0 9 0 9 8 6 4\n\nWait, but each is 9 digits (assuming commas are placed every three digits):\n\nWait 405,113,796 is:\n\n4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions),5 (millions),\n\n1 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),\n\n7 (hundreds),9 (tens),6 (units).\n\nSimilarly, 730,909,864:\n\n7 (hundred millions),3 (ten millions),0 (millions),\n\n9 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),\n\n8 (hundreds),6 (tens),4 (units).\n\nNow, adding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n6 +4 =10 \u21920, carry 1.\n\nTens:9 +6=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nHundreds:7 +8=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nThousands:3 +9=12 +1=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:1 +0=1 +1=2 \u21922, carry0.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +9=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nMillions:5 +0=5 +1=6 \u21926, carry0.\n\nTen millions:0 +3=3 \u21923, carry0.\n\nHundred millions:4 +7=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nBillions: carry1 \u21921.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:3,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nHundred thousands:0,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:3,\n\nHundreds:6,\n\nTens:6,\n\nUnits:0.\n\nThus the number is 1,136,023,660.\n\nAh, okay, so I had miscalculated earlier when I did the digit-by-digit because I might have miscounted the places. So the correct total is 1,136,023,660.\n\nVerifying with the calculator approach:\n\n405,113,796 + 730,909,864:\n\n405,113,796 +700,000,000 =1,105,113,796\n\nAdding remaining 30,909,864:\n\n1,105,113,796 +30,000,000 =1,135,113,796\n\nThen +909,864: 1,135,113,796 +909,864 =1,136,023,660. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo the correct answer is 1,136,023,660.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, 405,113,796 +730,909,864.\n\nAdding 400,000,000 +700,000,000 =1,100,000,000.\n\nThen 5,113,796 +30,909,864 =36,023,660.\n\nAdding that to 1,100,000,000 gives 1,136,023,660. Perfect.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 1,136,023,660.\n\nBut let me ensure that the commas are correctl