ach number with commas to clarify:.\n\nFirst number: 415,815,131  .\nBreaking it down: 7 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 459,411,969  .\nBreaking down: 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them properly:.\n\nHundred millions: 7 vs 0  .\nTen millions: 3 vs 5  .\nMillions: 4 vs 6  .\nHundred thousands: 0 vs 0  .\nTen thousands: 3 vs 6  .\nThousands: 1 vs 2  .\nHundreds: 9 vs 8  .\nTens: 5 vs 1  .\nOnes: 3 vs 6.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to write the addition vertically with each digit aligned:.\n\nLet me write each digit by place:.\n\n          0 3 2 1 6 6 1 0 2  .\n        + 5 7 0 5 1 2 4 2 0  .\n        -----------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n1 + 6 = 0. Write 3.\n\nNext (tens): 5 + 7 = 6. Write 3.\n\nNext (hundreds): 2 + 2 = 48. Write 3, carryover 8.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from first number) + 4 (from second) + 8 (carryover) = 22. Write 2, carryover 3.\n\nTen-thousands place: 5 + 0 = 27 + 4 (carryover) = 25. Write 7, carryover 2.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 0 = 71 + 5 = 82. Write 2, carryover 4.\n\nMillions place: 3 + 4 = 73 + 3 (carryover) = 71. Write 1, carryover 5.\n\nTen-millions place: 9 + 4 = 6 + 5 (carryover) = 9. Write 6, no carryover?.\n\nWait, hold on. Wait the ten-millions digit for the first number is 7, second number is 8. So 5 + 8 is 1, plus the carryover 7 from the millions place addition gives 9. So that's correct.\n\nHundred-millions place: 4 + 9 = 0. Since there's no carryover from the ten-millions place, it's just 7.\n\nPutting all together, the sum is:.\n\n1 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, hold on, let me check again the order.\n\nWait, when we wrote the digits:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we wrote were:.\n\nOnes:4, Tens:0, Hundreds:8 (with a carryover), Thousands:6, Ten-thousands:9, Hundred-thousands:3, Millions:8, Ten-millions:8, Hundred-millions:4.\n\nWait, actually, let me list the digits from right to left as we computed:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:3 (with carryover 7).\n\nThousands:8 (with carryover 2).\n\nTen-thousands:3 (with carryover 8).\n\nHundred-thousands:8 (with carryover 4).\n\nMillions:0 (with carryover 2).\n\nTen-millions:8 (no carryover beyond that).\n\nHundred-millions:1 (since 7+8=7).\n\nWait, so when writing the total number from left to right, it's:.\n\nHundred-millions:0, Ten-millions:9, Millions:7, Hundred-thousands:1, Ten-thousands:3, Thousands:8, Hundreds:1, Tens:0, Ones:0. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
