nds),9 (thousands),6 (hundreds),0 (tens),6 (ones).\n\nSo that's 579,129,606. Wait, so why did my previous method give 579,129,706?\n\nAh, because in that other method I added 331,218,517 + 247,911,189 as:\n\nFirst adding 331,218,517 + 200,000,000 =531,218,517.\n\nThen adding47,911,189: 531,218,517 +47,911,189.\n\nWait 47,911,189 is 40,000,000 +7,911,189.\n\nAdding 40,000,000:531,218,517 +40,000,000 =571,218,517.\n\nThen add7,911,189:\n\n571,218,517 +7,000,000 =578,218,517.\n\nThen add911,189:\n\n578,218,517 +911,189 =579,129,706.\n\nWait, but according to digit-by-digit it's 579,129,606. There's a difference of 100 in the hundreds place. So where is the error?\n\nWait let's compute 578,218,517 +911,189 step by step:\n\n578,218,517 +911,189.\n\nBreakdown:\n\nFirst add 578,218,517 + 900,000 =579,118,517.\n\nThen add 11,189:\n\n579,118,517 +10,000 =579,128,517.\n\nThen add1,189:\n\n579,128,517 +1,189 =579,129,706.\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit, it should be 579,129,606. So discrepancy of 100. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe the digit-by-digit had an error?\n\nWait let's do the digit-by-digit again, carefully:\n\nPosition1:7+9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nPosition2:1 (first's tens) +8 (second's tens) +1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nPosition3:5 (first's hundreds) +1 (second's hundreds) +0=6 \u21926.\n\nPosition4:8 (first's thousands) +1 (second's thousands) =9.\n\nPosition5:1 (first's ten thousands) +1 (second's ten thousands)=2.\n\nPosition6:2 (first's hundred thousands) +9 (second's hundred thousands)=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nPosition7:1 (first's millions) +7 (second's millions) +1=9.\n\nPosition8:3 (first's ten millions) +4 (second's ten millions)=7.\n\nPosition9:3 +2=5.\n\nSo the total digits:\n\nPosition9:5, Position8:7, Position7:9, Position6:1, Position5:2, Position4:9, Position3:6, Position2:0, Position1:6.\n\nSo the number is 579,129,606.\n\nBut when adding through the other way, it's 579,129,706. There must be a miscalculation in one of the methods.\n\nWait let me compute using 