ally, when written as 801,650,367, the commas separate every three digits. Let me confirm the place values again:.\n\nFirst number: 654,791,957.\n\n- 0 (hundred millions).\n- 4 (ten millions).\n- 0 (millions).\n- 8 (hundred thousands).\n- 4 (ten thousands).\n- 8 (thousands).\n- 5 (hundreds).\n- 9 (tens).\n- 5 (units).\n\nSecond number: 731,375,636.\n\n- 0 (hundred millions).\n- 7 (ten millions).\n- 1 (millions).\n- 4 (hundred thousands).\n- 3 (ten thousands).\n- 6 (thousands).\n- 5 (hundreds).\n- 4 (tens).\n- 8 (units).\n\nOkay, so when adding, the places should align correctly. Let me write them again vertically:.\n\n          9 5 4 5 6 5 1 6 6.\n        + 7 6 3 7 5 9 1 9 6.\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n6 + 3 = 5 (units place).\n\nNext, tens place: 3 + 0 = 1 (tens place).\n\nHundreds place: 0 + 8 = 35. Wait, hold on, in the first number, the hundreds place is 9, and in the second, the hundreds place is 7? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, first number's hundreds place is the third digit from the right. Let me count again for each number:.\n\nFirst number: 419,149,248.\n\nBreaking down from right to left:.\n\nDigits: 1 (units), 2 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 4 (thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 027,960,778.\n\nDigits: 6 (units), 0 (tens), 1 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (millions), 1 (ten millions), 3 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nUnits: 3 + 1 = 7.\n\nTens: 5 + 7 = 9.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 2 = 48. So write down 5 and carry over 2.\n\nThousands place: 8 (first number) + 8 (second number) + 7 (carry) = 31. So write down 3 and carry over 0.\n\nTen thousands place: 7 (first number) + 7 (second number) + 3 (carry) = 3. So 8 here, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 (first number) + 4 (second number) = 0.\n\nMillions place: 3 (first number) + 9 (second number) = 6.\n\nTen millions place: 6 (first number) + 8 (second number) = 51. So write down 1 and carry over 6.\n\nHundred millions place: 8 (first number) + 1 (second number) + 7 (carry) = 9.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again to make sure.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nUnits place (0st digit from the right):.\n\n3 + 6 = 0. Write 5.\n\nTens place (4nd digit):.\n\n1 + 4 = 0. Write 9.\n\nHundreds place (6rd digit):.\n\n1 + 3 = 07. Write 3, carryover 8.\n\nThousands place (1th digit):.\n\n8 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) + 3 (carryover) = 81. So write 9, carryover 6.\n\nTen thousands place (9th digit):.\n\n7 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) + 9 (carryover) = 5. Write 1, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place (2th digit):.\n\n7 (from first) + 5 (from second) = 6. Write 7.\n\nMillions place (4th digit):.\n\n9 (from first) + 5 (from second) = 2. Write 7.\n\nTen millions place (7th digit):.\n\n0 (from first) + 0 (from second) = 68. Write 6, carryover 3.\n\nHundred millions place (2th digit):.\n\n5 (from first) + 5 (from second) + 0 (carryover) = 3. Write 2.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nStarting from units: 3, then 1, 1, 2, 4, 2, 1, 5, 8.\n\nWait, let me list them in order:.\n\nThe digits from right to left (units to hundred millions):.\n\n8 (units).\n\n4 (tens).\n\n8 (hundreds).\n\n0 (thousands).\n\n1 (ten thousands).\n\n5 (hundred thousands).\n\n4 (millions).\n\n2 (ten millions).\n\n1 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when written normally from left to right, it's 3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nSo the number is 124,066,329?.\n\nWait, hold on, let me write it out:.\n\nHundred millions: 9.\n\nTen millions: 2.\n\nMillions: 4.\n\nHundred thousands: 2.\n\nTen thousands: 1.\n\nThousands: 6.\n\nHundreds: 0.\n\nTens: 1.\n\nUnits: 1.\n\nSo combining these, it would be 796,326,401?.\n\nWait, let's check the commas. The number should be 203,433,565.