lace: 6 (first) + 6 (second) = 76 → 5, carryover 8.\n\n2. Hundred-millions place: 7 (first) + 1 (second) = 67 + 6 (carryover) = 04 → 4, carryover 4.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 8 becomes a new digit at the billions place.\n\nSo the total digits from right to left would be:.\n\nUnits:5, Tens:1, Hundreds:7, Thousands:9, Ten-thousands:1, Hundred-thousands:7, Millions:0, Ten-millions:5, Hundred-millions:9, and the final carryover 0 in the billions place.\n\nPutting all together from left to right (billions, hundred millions, ten millions, etc.):.\n\n2 (billions), 7 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 4 (units).\n\nWait, let me structure that properly. The digits from the highest place to the lowest:.\n\nStarting with the carryover 5, then the hundred-millions digit (9), ten-millions (5), millions (8), hundred-thousands (6), ten-thousands (0), thousands (8), hundreds (5), tens (3), units (4). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
