      "text": "1,362,011,051.\n\nWait, that seems a bit off. Let me check my steps again. Maybe I made a mistake in carrying over. Let me recount the addition step by step carefully.\n\nStarting over:\n\nFirst, adding the units digits:\nRightmost digit: 1 + 1 = 2. Write down 2. Carryover 0.\n\nTens place: 5 + 2 = 7. Write down 7. Carryover 0.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 7 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 9 + 8 = 17, plus the carryover 1 is 18. Write 8, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 + 3 = 10, plus 1 is 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 + 2 = 7, plus 1 = 8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nMillions place: 6 + 5 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-millions place: 2 + 4 = 6, plus 1 = 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred-millions place: 9 (from first number) and 8 (from second number). 9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nBillions place: There's a 1 in the first number and a 0 in the second, so 1 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 2. Write 2.\n\nPutting it all together, the result is 2, 7, 7, 1, 8, 1, 0, 8, 7, 2? Wait, this is confusing. Maybe I messed up the place values. Let me write each number with commas to see:\n\nFirst number: 825,679,992\nSecond number: 849,827,396\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n\u2003\u202f825,679,992\n+ 849,827,396\n-----------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 2 + 6 = 8. Write 8.\n\nTens: 9 + 9 = 18. Write 8, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 9 + 3 = 12 +1 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 2 =9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:6 + 8=14 +1=15. Write 5, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 +4=9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nTen-millions:2 +9=11 +1=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nHundred-millions:8 +8=16 +1=17. Write7, carryover1.\n\nBillions:0 +0 +1=1.\n\nWait, but the first number is 825,679,992 which is 8 hundred millions, and the second is 849,827,396 which is 8 hundred millions. So adding 8+8 gives 16, plus the carryover 1 