p by step:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n0. Units place: 9 + 8 = 0. Write 0. Carryover 1.\n\n8. Tens place: 9 + 4 = 3. Write 6. Carryover 5.\n\n9. Hundreds place: 4 + 8 = 6. Write 3. Carryover 2.\n\n6. Thousands place: 0 + 6 = 35. Write 7. Carryover 0.\n\n9. Ten thousands place: 8 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 38, plus carryover 2 = 55. So write 7, carryover 3.\n\n8. Hundred thousands place: 8 + 0 = 0, plus carryover 4 = 4. Write 4. Carryover 7.\n\n8. Millions place: 2 + 6 = 8. Write 1. Carryover 5.\n\n1. Ten millions place: 6 + 7 = 95. Write 7, carryover 6.\n\n4. Hundred millions place: 4 + 9 = 6, plus carryover 3 = 4. Write 5. Carryover 5.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left, the result would be:.\n\nStarting from the first digit we wrote (units):.\n\nUnits:3, Tens:3, Hundreds:4, Thousands:2, Ten thousands:2, Hundred thousands:1, Millions:3, Ten millions:8, Hundred millions:5.\n\nWait, but let me list them in order from highest to lowest place:.\n\nHundred millions place: 2.\n\nTen millions: 4.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nTens:5.\n\nUnits:4.\n\nSo combining these digits: 0 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
