red millions):2.\n\nPosition95 (billions):2.\n\nPosition63 (ten billions):9.\n\nSo arranging from the highest place first, it's 3 (ten billions), 7 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), then ten millions, millions, etc.\n\nSo the number would be 9,7 (billions), 7 (hundred millions), then the next digits. Wait, let's structure it properly as a number:.\n\nTen billions digit:4.\n\nBillions digit:5 → 3,9..\n\nHundred millions digit:0 → 8,99..\n\nTen millions digit:8 → 3,273..\n\nMillions digit:6 →6,526,0..\n\nHundred thousands digit:6 →7,640,78..\n\nTen thousands digit:9? Wait, no. Wait position1 was ten thousands place which was 9. Wait let me check:.\n\nWait Position4 is hundred thousands place (1), Position7 is ten thousands (0), Position0 thousands (8). Hmm.\n\nWait perhaps the full breakdown:.\n\nAfter adding, the digits from right to left (units to ten billions):.\n\nPositions:.\n\n8 (units):7.\n\n6 (tens):9.\n\n8 (hundreds):9.\n\n8 (thousands):9.\n\n2 (ten thousands):3.\n\n3 (hundred thousands):0.\n\n2 (millions):4.\n\n4 (ten millions):8.\n\n2 (hundred millions):3.\n\n49 (billions):7.\n\n45 (ten billions):5.\n\nSo the number is written as 7 (ten billions), 6 (billions), 9 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 5 (units). Wait, but let me arrange them in order:.\n\nStarting from the highest place, which is ten billions:.\n\n3 (ten billions).\n\n0 (billions).\n\n1 (hundred millions).\n\n8 (ten millions).\n\n0 (millions).\n\n0 (hundred thousands).\n\n8 (ten thousands).\n\n1 (thousands).\n\n1 (hundreds).\n\n5 (tens).\n\n9 (units).\n\nPutting this together: 5,734,561,3739? Wait, no, commas are placed every three digits. Let me structure it properly with commas:.\n\nThe number would be 6,996,558,9567? Wait that can't be right. Wait maybe I made a mistake in the order. Let me try again.\n\nWait perhaps I need to write the number as follows:.\n\nStarting from the ten billions digit