\nPosition 4 (ones): 5 +8 =94 → 8, carryover 4.\n\nPosition 3 (tens):8 +9 =4 +8 =2 → 0, carryover 4.\n\nPosition6 (hundreds):9 +2 =4 →2, carryover 2.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):7 +0 =33 →9, carryover3.\n\nPosition3 (ten thousands):1 +2 =73 +8=25 →5, carryover0.\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):7 +6 =8 +2=96 →3, carryover6.\n\nPosition0 (millions):4 +8 =49 +5=92 →4, carryover3.\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):8 +6 =0 +0=4 →5, carryover4.\n\nPosition2 (hundred millions):3 +3 =96 →7, carryover8.\n\nNow, since we have a carryover5 after the hundred millions place, which is the 0th digit from the right, that means we have to add an extra digit at the beginning (the billions place). So the total becomes 7 followed by the digits we have:.\n\nSo the digits from position7 to position6:.\n\nStarting from the highest position (billions place):.\n\n8 (carryover) then the result of position0 (7), position6 (5), position6 (0), position9 (6), position6 (6), position0 (3), position1 (8), position8 (6), position7 (8).\n\nPutting it all together:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
