0+6=50 →6, carryover9.\n\nTens:7+2=0 +4=5.\n\nUnits:6+9=2.\n\nWait, so the sum is 6,089,075. Wait, how?.\n\nWait let me do it step by step:.\n\n466,009 + 762,236:.\n\nStart from right:.\n\nUnits:0+1=3.\n\nTens:4+4=1.\n\nHundreds:0+0=49 →7, carryover8.\n\nThousands:0 (from first number) +0 (second) +2 =2.\n\nTen thousands:5 (first) +2 (second) =89 →1, carryover2.\n\nHundred thousands:4 (first) +2 (second) =53 +3 (carryover) =36 →0, carryover2.\n\nBut since there are no more digits, the carryover8 becomes a new digit at the millions place.\n\nSo total is 9,929,723. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
