al numbers again.\n\nWait, the first number is 328,739,002. Breaking down each digit:\n\n- Hundreds millions place: 3 (since 3 is the first digit, representing 300,000,000).\n\n- Ten millions place: 2 (20,000,000).\n\n- Millions place:8 (8,000,000).\n\n- Hundred thousands place:7 (700,000).\n\n- Ten thousands place:3 (30,000).\n\n- Thousands place:9 (9,000).\n\n- Hundreds place:0 (0).\n\n- Tens place:0 (0).\n\n- Units place:2 (2).\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I misaligned the digits earlier. Let me do this more carefully.\n\nBreaking down 328,739,002:\n\nDigits from left to right (hundred millions down to units):\n\n3 (hundred millions)\n\n2 (ten millions)\n\n8 (millions)\n\n7 (hundred thousands)\n\n3 (ten thousands)\n\n9 (thousands)\n\n0 (hundreds)\n\n0 (tens)\n\n2 (units)\n\nSimilarly, the second number 386,190,257:\n\n3 (hundred millions)\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n6 (millions)\n\n1 (hundred thousands)\n\n9 (ten thousands)\n\n0 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n5 (tens)\n\n7 (units)\n\nWait, let's verify:\n\n386,190,257:\n\n- 3 (hundred millions: 300,000,000)\n\n- 8 (ten millions: 80,000,000)\n\n- 6 (millions: 6,000,000)\n\n- 1 (hundred thousands: 100,000)\n\n- 9 (ten thousands: 90,000)\n\n- 0 (thousands: 0)\n\n- 2 (hundreds: 200)\n\n- 5 (tens: 50)\n\n- 7 (units:7)\n\nNow, aligning the two numbers:\n\nFirst number (328,739,002):\n\nPositions (from right, units to hundred millions):\n\nPosition 1 (units): 2\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 0\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):0\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):9\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):3\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):7\n\nPosition 7 (millions):8\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):2\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):3\n\nSecond number (386,190,257):\n\nPosition1 (units):7\n\nPosition2 (tens):5\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1\n\nPosition7 (millions):6\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):8\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3\n\nNow, adding each position from right to left:\n\nPosition1 (units): 2 +7 =9. Write 9.\n\nPosition2 (tens):0 +5=5. Write5.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0 +2=2. Write2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9 +0=9. Write9.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3 +9=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):7 +1 +1 (carryover)=9. Write9, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (millions):8 +6=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2 +8 +1 (carryover)=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3 +3 +1 (carryover)=7. Write7.\n\nSo putting all digits together from position9 to position1:\n\n7 (hundred millions)\n\n1 (ten millions)\n\n4 (millions)\n\n9 (hundred thousands)\n\n2 (ten thousands)\n\n9 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n5 (tens)\n\n9 (units)\n\nWait, let me list them in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:5\n\nUnits:9\n\nSo writing the number as: 714,929,259.\n\nWait, let me construct the number properly:\n\nStarting from the highest place:\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:1 \u2192 710,000,000\n\nMillions:4 \u2192 adding 4,000,000 \u2192 714,000,000\n\nHundred thousands:9 \u2192 900,000 \u2192 total 714,900,000\n\nTen thousands:2 \u2192 20,000 \u2192 714,920,000\n\nThousands:9 \u2192 9,000 \u2192 714,929,000\n\nHundreds:2 \u2192 200 \u2192 714,929,200\n\nTens:5 \u2192 50 \u2192 714,929,250\n\nUnits:9 \u2192 714,929,259.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 714,929,259.\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers numerically:\n\n328,739,002\n\n+386,190,257\n\n-------------\n\nAdding step by step:\n\nStart with 328,739,002 + 386,190,257.\n\nAdd the millions first:\n\n328,000,000 + 386,000,000 = 714,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n739,002 + 190,257 = ?\n\n739,002 + 190,257.\n\nAdding 700,000 + 100,000 = 800,000.\n\n39,002 + 90,257 = 129,259.\n\nWait, so total would be 800,000 + 129,259 = 929,259.\n\nHence, total sum is 714,000,000 + 929,259 = 714,929,259. That matches the previous result.\n\nSo I think that's correct. Therefore, the answer is 714,929,259.\n\nBut let me check once more with another approach, maybe breaking down the numbers into parts.\n\n328,739,002 can be written as 300,000,000 + 28,000,000 + 700,000 + 30,000 + 9,000 + 0 + 0 + 2.\n\nSimilarly, 386,190,257 is 300,000,000 + 80,000,000 + 6,000,000 + 100,000 + 90,000 + 0 + 200 + 50 +7.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n300M + 300M = 600M.\n\n28M +80M =108M \u2192 total 600+108=708M.\n\n700k +6,000,000 = 6,700,000 \u2192 adding to 708M gives 714.7M? Wait, perhaps better to do each term:\n\nWait maybe this is getting too convoluted, but since the previous two methods gave me the same answer, I can be confident.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like addition:\n\n328,739,002\n\n+386,190,257\n\nStart from the right:\n\nAdding units place:2 +7=9\n\nTens:0+5=5\n\nHundreds:0+2=2\n\nThousands:9+0=9\n\nTen thousands:3+9=12 (carryover1)\n\nHundred thousands:7+1=8 +1=9\n\nMillions:8+6=14 (carryover1)\n\nTen millions:2+8=10 +1=11 (carryover1)\n\nHundred millions:3+3=6 +1=7.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nUnits:9\n\nTens:5\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen thousands:2 (with a carryover)\n\nWait, but in the ten thousands place, 3+9=12, so write 2 and carryover 1 to hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place:7+1=8 plus the carryover 1 makes 9.\n\nMillions place:8+6=14, so write 4 and carryover 1.\n\nTen millions place:2+8=10 plus carryover1 makes 11, so write 1 and carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:3+3=6 plus carryover1 makes 7.\n\nThus the result is 714,929,259. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the correct sum is 714,929,259.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 328739002 and 386190257 is \\boxed{714929259}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 328,739,002 and 386,190,257, we align the numbers by their place values and add each column from right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  328,739,002 \\\\\n+ 386,