er 1 \u219215. Write down 5, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place:0 +8=8 plus carryover 1 \u21929. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:7 +9=16. Write 6, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions place:2 +8=10 plus carryover1 \u219211. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nFinally, the carryover 1 becomes the billions place.\n\nSo the total is 1 (billion), 1 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions?), let's see:\n\nPutting the digits together from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:4\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:8\n\nSo combining these:\n\n1 (billion), 1 (hundred million), 6 (ten million), 9 (million), 5 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 4 (hundred), 3 (ten), 8 (one).\n\nTherefore, the number is 1,169,536,438.\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\nBreaking down the digits as per place:\n\n1,169,536,438.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n1,169,536,438.\n\n1 billion,\n\n169 million,\n\n536 thousand,\n\n438.\n\nLet me add the two original numbers numerically:\n\n270,665,636\n\n+898,870,802\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\n270,665,636\n\n+800,000,000 = 1,070,665,636\n\nNow add 98,870,802:\n\n1,070,665,636 + 98,870,802 = ?\n\n1,070,665,636 + 90,000,000 = 1,160,665,636\n\nThen add 8,870,802:\n\n1,160,665,636 + 8,000,000 = 1,168,665,636\n\nThen + 870,802:\n\n1,168,665,636 + 870,802 = 1,169,536,438.\n\nYes, that matches. So the correct answer is 1,169,536,438.\n\nTherefore, after going through the step-by-step addition and verifying with an alternative method, I conclude that the sum of 270,665,636 and 898,870,802 is 1,169,536,438.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 270665636 and 898870802 is \\boxed{1169536438}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem of adding 270,665,636 and 898,870,802, we start by aligning the numbers vertically and adding each column from right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  270,665,636 \\\\\n+ 898,870,802 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n- Ones place: \\(6 + 2 = 8\\)\n- Tens place: \\(3 + 0 = 3\\)\n- Hundreds place: \\(6 + 8 = 14\\) (write down 4, carry over 1)\n- Thousands place: \\(5 + 0 + 1 = 6\\) (carry over 0)\n- Ten thousands place: \\(6 + 7 = 13\\) (write down 3, carry over 1)\n- Hundred thousands place: \\(6 + 8 + 1 = 15\\) (write down 5, carry over 1)\n- Millions place: \\(0 + 8 + 1 = 9\\) (carry over 0)\n- Ten millions place: \\(7 + 9 = 16\\) (write down 6, carry over 1)\n- Hundred millions place: \\(2 + 8 + 1 = 11\\) (write down 1, carry over 1)\n- Billions place: 1 (from the carry over)\n\nCombining all the digits from left to right, we get the result:\n\n\\[\n1,169,536,438\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of 270,665,636 and 898,870,802 is \\(\\boxed{1169536438}\\).",
