  ----------------.\n\nAligning them properly:.\n\n        836,780,600.\n      + 371,099,680.\n      =============.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits place: 0 + 6 = 5 ✔️.\n\nTens place: 9 + 5 = 4 ✔️.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 5 = 47. Write 2, carryover 9. ✔️.\n\nThousands place: 0 + 0 = 2, plus the carried 4 is 1 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands place: 5 + 4 = 2 ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands place: 0 + 8 = 4 ✔️.\n\nMillions place: 0 + 0 = 38. Write 5, carryover 7. ✔️.\n\nTen millions place: 0 + 0 = 3, plus the carried 9 makes 31. Write 2, carryover 4. ✔️.\n\nHundred millions place: 4 + 4 = 97, plus the carried 9 makes 25. Write 1, carryover 2. ✔️.\n\nBillions place: The first number has 2 (since it\'s 932 million, so the billions digit is 4?), wait hold on. Wait, 911,759,117 is 9 hundred million, 36 million, etc. Wait, actually, breaking it down:.\n\n474,110,871 is:.\n\n- 1 (hundred millions).\n- 2 (ten millions).\n- 2 (millions).\n- 8 (hundred thousands).\n- 2 (ten thousands).\n- 5 (thousands).\n- 7 (hundreds).\n- 8 (tens).\n- 1 (units).\n\nWait, actually, maybe my place breakdown is off. Let me confirm the places properly. Let me write the number with commas as thousand separators. The number 725,810,053 is:.\n\nBreaking down the commas: the first comma from the right separates thousands, the next separates millions, etc. So:.\n\n969,889,255 is 890 million, 771 thousand, 729. So the digits are:.\n\nBillions place: 8 (since 133 million is 9.8 billion).\n\nWait actually, 819 million is 6.140 billion. So the digits are:.\n\n- Billions place: 7 (since 474,656,344).\n- Hundred millions: 6 (78,228,591).\n- Ten millions: 5 (8,119,558).\n- Millions: 7 (659,715).\nWait, no, actually, the way numbers are broken down:.\n\nEach comma represents a thousand separators. So starting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 7.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nBillions:2? Wait, 528,620,616. The first c