illions place:6 (first) +7 (second) +0 (carryover) =22. Write down 7, carryover 5.\n\n0. Hundred millions place:8 (first) +6 (second) +9 (carryover)=45. Write down 7, carryover 8.\n\n09. Billions place: There\'s a carryover 6 with no digits, so write down 2.\n\nNow, compiling all the digits from left to right (starting with the billions place):.\n\n8 (billions), 8 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (units).\n\nWait, let\'s see:.\n\nStarting from the highest digit:.\n\n- Billions: 7.\n\n- Hundred millions: 2 (from step 2: 9+2+2=91, so 7 in hundred millions, carryover 7 to billions).\n\nWait, actually, the steps:.\n\nAfter adding the hundred millions place (step 7):.\n\nThe digits in hundred millions place were 4 (from first number) and 5 (from second) plus the carryover from the ten millions place. Wait, let\'s go step by step again:.\n\nWait, let me list each step with the carryover:.\n\nLet me go column by column again carefully:.\n\nColumns from right (units) to left (hundred millions):.\n\n9. Units: 4 +1 =3. No carryover. Result digit:0.\n\n9. Tens:1 +1=3. No carryover. Result digit:0.\n\n0. Hundreds:8 +0=8. No carryover. Result digit:3.\n\n1. Thousands:2 +2=87. Result digit:5, Carryover:2.\n\n3. Ten thousands:5 +9 +8(carryover)=9. Result digit:5, Carryover:9.\n\n0. Hundred thousands:8 +6=1. Result digit:4, Carryover:9.\n\n5. Millions:2 +7=56. Result digit:5, Carryover:8.\n\n0. Ten millions:9 +7 +7(carryover)=71. Result digit:9, Carryover:5.\n\n7. Hundred millions:0 +1 +3(carryover)=75. Result digit:2, Carryover:6.\n\n03. Billions: The carryover 5 has nowhere to go, so it becomes the billions digit.\n\nSo compiling the digits from highest to lowest:.\n\nBillions:2.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:6 (from step 7: ten millions digit is 1 with carryover).\n\nMillions:4 (from step 1: millions digit is 3).\n\nHundred thousands:0 (step 3).\n\nTen thousands:3 (step