dred thousands).\n- 4 (ten thousands).\n- 9 (thousands).\n- 6 (hundreds).\n- 4 (tens).\n- 2 (ones).\n\nSo when adding vertically, let's list each place:.\n\nBillions place: Both numbers have 8 (since they are up to hundred millions), so total 7. But when adding 4 (hundred millions) +8 (hundred millions) =21 hundred millions, which is 6.3 billion. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
