red thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds),5 (tens),7 (ones). So the number is 881,511,657. Yes, that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 881,511,657.\n\nBut just to be absolutely sure, let me use another method. Let me add the two numbers in parts.\n\nFirst, let's split the numbers into millions, thousands, and units.\n\nFirst number:469,821,234\n\nThis can be broken down as:\n\n400,000,000 + 69,821,234\n\nSecond number:411,690,423\n\nWhich is 400,000,000 + 11,690,423\n\nAdding the millions parts first:\n\n400M +400M=800M.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n69,821,234 +11,690,423.\n\nAdding those:\n\n69,821,234\n\n+11,690,423\n\n= (60,000,000 +9,000,000 +800,000 +20,000 +1,000 +200 +30 +4)\n\n+ (10,000,000 +1,000,000 +600,000 +90,000 +400 +20 +3)\n\nBut maybe adding step by step:\n\n69,821,234\n\n+11,690,423\n\nStart with the millions:\n\n60,000,000 +10,000,000 =70,000,000\n\n9,000,000 +1,000,000=10,000,000 \u2192 total so far 80,000,000\n\nThen 800,000 +600,000 =1,400,000 \u2192 total 81,400,000.\n\nThen 20,000 +90,000 =110,000 \u2192 total 81,510,000.\n\nThen 1,000 +0 \u219281,511,000.\n\n200 +400 =600 \u219281,511,600.\n\n30 +20 =50 \u219281,511,650.\n\n4 +3 =7 \u219281,511,657.\n\nAdding this to the 800M gives 800,000,000 +81,511,657 =881,511,657.\n\nSame result. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like step:\n\n469,821,234\n\n+411,690,423\n\n= (469,821,234 + 400,000,000) = 869,821,234 ?\n\nWait no, that's not the way. Let me do it step by step:\n\nStart with 469,821,234\n\nAdd 400,000,000 \u2192 869,821,234\n\nThen add 11,690,423.\n\nAdding 869,821,234 +10,000,000 =879,821,234\n\nThen add 1,690,423.\n\n879,821,234 +1,000,000 =880,821,234\n\n+690,423:\n\n880,821,234 +600,000 =881,421,234\n\n+90,423:\n\n881,421,234 +90,000 =881,511,234\n\n+423 =881,511,657.\n\nYup, same result again. So I'm confident that the correct sum is 881,511,657.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 881,511,657.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 46