 up the order earlier. Let me start over and align each digit properly:.\n\nFirst number: 965,039,423.\nSecond number: 392,763,384.\n\nLet me write them aligned:.\n\n        3 3 6 1 0 9 5 4 8.\n      + 7 5 2 7 3 1 0 7 3.\n      ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 3 + 3 = 66. Write 1, carryover 4.\n\nTens: 5 + 4 = 75, plus 9 is 01. Write 9, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 6 = 8, plus 7 is 5. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 4 + 6 = 2. Write 7.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 + 8 = 2. Write 6.\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 3 = 3. Write 8.\n\nMillions: 9 + 2 = 43. Wait, hold on. Wait, the millions place in the first number is 5 (since 395,703,606 is 0 hundred million, 9 ten million, 9 million, etc.), and the second number is 614,457,663, which has 0 in the millions place (since it's 0 hundred million, 4 ten million, 8 million). So adding millions: 3 + 4 = 79. So write 7 and carryover 7.\n\nTen-millions place: 0 (from first number) + 0 (from second) = 2, plus the carryover 8 makes 2. Write 7.\n\nHundred-millions place: 2 + 8 = 50. Write 7 and carryover 5.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 6 becomes the next digit. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
