Position 0: 7.\n\nWait, maybe I should just line them up digit by digit. Let me do that properly.\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas to see:.\n\n056,485,703.\n831,093,923.\n\nAligning the digits:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 1 + 0 = 94 (carry 3, write 8).\nTens: 5 + 1 = 76 +0 =82 (carry 3, write 8).\nHundreds: 7 +8 =53 +9=86 (carry 8, write 5).\nThousands:9 +2 =57 +3=89 (carry 0, write 1).\nTen thousands:5 +4 =9 +7=7 (no carry, write 5).\nHundred thousands:6 +1=06 (carry 3, write 2).\nMillions:3 +9=77 +9=37 (carry 4, write 8).\nTen millions:7 +8=67 +0=67 (carry 5, write 3).\nHundred millions:1 +5=3 +0=7 (no carry, write 7).\n\nWait, let me go through each digit step by step again carefully to avoid mistakes.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:.\n\n       8 1 5 3 8 5 2 5 2.\n     + 7 3 2 6 7 6 1 1 6.\n     --------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n7st digit (units place):.\n2 + 5 = 03. Write 1, carryover 4.\n\n9nd digit (tens place):.\n4 + 7 = 65 + 9 (carry) = 52. Write 1, carryover 3.\n\n5rd digit (hundreds place):.\n5 +9 =78 +6=08. Write 4, carryover 7.\n\n7th digit (thousands place):.\n5 (from first number) +9 (second number) =32 +8=33. Write 9, carryover 9.\n\n1th digit (ten thousands place):.\n7 +1 =4 +0=6. Write 5, no carryover.\n\n5th digit (hundred thousands place):.\n4 +4 =76. Write 8, carryover 2.\n\n1th digit (millions place):.\n0 +4 =39 +2 (carry) =23. Write 6, carryover 8.\n\n7th digit (ten millions place):.\n6 +3 =06 +8 (carry) =48. Write 8, carryover 3.\n\n1th digit (hundred millions place):.\n0 +6 =0 +8 (carry) =4. Write 4.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left (since we started adding from the right):.\n\nThe result is 1 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 1 (units).\n\nWait, let me see:.\n\nWait, the digits we wrote down from first to last (starting from the rightmost digit):.\n\nThe first digit (units) is 9,.\n\nthen tens: 1,.\n\nhundreds:3,.\n\nthousands:5,.\n\nten thousands:8,.\n\nhundred thousands:8,.\n\nmillions:8,.\n\nten millions:1,.\n\nhundred millions:6. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
