\n\n------------\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n338,712,736\n\n+377,849,524\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 6 + 4 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nTens place: 3 + 2 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 9 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 + 4 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 8 = 15. Write 5, carry over 1.\n\nMillions place: 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry over 1.\n\nTen millions place: 3 + 3 = 6 + 1 (carry) = 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place: 3 + 3 = 6. Write 6.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again:\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nFirst number: 338,712,736\n\nDigits:\n\nHundred millions: 3\n\nTen millions: 3\n\nMillions: 8\n\nHundred thousands: 7\n\nTen thousands: 1\n\nThousands: 2\n\nHundreds: 7\n\nTens: 3\n\nOnes: 6\n\nSecond number: 377,849,524\n\nDigits:\n\nHundred millions: 3\n\nTen millions: 7\n\nMillions: 7\n\nHundred thousands: 8\n\nTen thousands: 4\n\nThousands: 9\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 4\n\nNow adding column by column:\n\nOnes: 6 + 4 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 3 + 2 = 5 + 1 = 6. Write 6, carry 0.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 2 + 9 = 11 + 1 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 1 + 4 = 5 + 1 = 6. Write 6, carry 0.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 8 = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nTen millions: 3 + 7 = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nHundred millions: 3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7. Write 7.\n\nWait, so putting the digits together from right to left:\n\nOnes: 0\n\nTens: 6\n\nHundreds: 2\n\nThousands: 2\n\nTen thousands: 6\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:1\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nWait, wait, let's list them in order from the right:\n\nOnes place: 0\n\nTens: 6\n\nHundreds: 2\n\nThousands: 2\n\nTen thousands: 6\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:1\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nSo the number would be 7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nWait, that's 716,562,260? Wait, let's see:\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:1 \u2192 710,000,000\n\nMillions:6 \u2192 716,000,000\n\nHundred thousands:5 \u2192 716,500,000\n\nTen thousands:6 \u2192716,560,000\n\nThousands:2 \u2192716,562,000\n\nHundreds:2 \u2192716,562,200\n\nTens:6 \u2192716,562,260\n\nOnes:0 \u2192716,562,260\n\nWait, but the ten millions place was 3 +7 (from the original numbers):\n\nWait, hold on, let me re-examine the Ten millions place addition:\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number's ten millions digit: 3\n\nSecond number's ten millions digit:7\n\nSo 3 +7 = 10, plus the carryover from millions place (which was 1 from the millions addition):\n\nWait, let me retrace the addition step for ten millions:\n\nMillions place addition was 8 (first number) +7 (second number) =15, plus carryover 1 from hundred thousands? Wait, let me redo the addition step by step again to avoid confusion.\n\nLet me write all digits with their place values:\n\nFirst number: 3 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 3 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions),7 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),5 (hundreds),2 (tens),4 (ones).\n\nNow, adding column by column starting from the right (ones):\n\nOnes digit: 6 +4 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 3 +2 =5 +1=6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds:7 +5=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nThousands:2 +9=11 +1=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:1 +4=5 +1=6. Write6, carryover0.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +8=15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nMillions:8 +7=15 +1=16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:3 +7=10 +1=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:3 +3=6 +1=7. Write7,