Write 1, carryover 5. Right.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from first number) + 4 (from second) plus carryover 4 = 5. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 9 = 1. Correct.\n\nMillions: 3 + 5 = 43. Write 4, carryover 4. Correct.\n\nTen-millions: 6 (from first) + 5 (from second) +7 (carryover) = 2. Correct.\n\nHundred-millions: 3 +5 =2. Correct. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
