n2 (millions):8.\n\n1 (ten millions):0.\n\n3 (hundred millions):3.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\n4. Units: 6 +0 =40. Write 7, carryover 9.\n\n9. Tens:2 +7 =0 +4=25. Write 8, carryover4.\n\n7. Hundreds:7 +8 =0 +0=0. Write1, no carryover.\n\n7. Thousands:9 +5=46. Write7, carryover2.\n\n0. Ten thousands:5 +7=27 +0=78. Write4, carryover4.\n\n3. Hundred thousands:8 +9=6 +5=5. Write4, no.\n\n8. Millions:1 +5=8. Write9.\n\n0. Ten millions:5 +5=02. Write7, carryover7.\n\n6. Hundred millions:1 +4=56 +0=36. Write3, carryover2.\n\nFinally, the carryover3 is added as the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo the result is 6 5 8 9 3 9 0 6 1 6.\n\nWait, but let me arrange the digits properly. Starting from the highest place, which is billions:.\n\nBillions place:3.\n\nThen hundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:3.\n\nUnits:7.\n\nWait, but when written out, that would be 8,124,215,387?.\n\nWait, let me check the digits again step by step:.\n\nAfter adding each place:.\n\n- Units digit:0.\n\n- Tens:9.\n\n- Hundreds:4.\n\n- Thousands:6.\n\n- Ten thousands:9.\n\n- Hundred thousands:5.\n\n- Millions:1.\n\n- Ten millions:1.\n\n- Hundred millions:3.\n\n- Billions:5.\n\nSo when written in order from highest to lowest place:.\n\nBillions (4), hundred millions (2), ten millions (2), millions (4), hundred thousands (6), ten thousands (8), thousands (9), hundreds (4), tens (2), units (8).\n\nSo combining those digits: 4 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (units). So the number is 7,754,304,527?.\n\nWait, let me write it with commas:.\n\nStarting from the right, every three digits:.\n\nThe digits are 3 3 0 0 3 3 5 1 4 8.\n\nBreaking into groups:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 0.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:5 → 931.\n\nThousands:8 → 9,640.\n\nTen thousands:9