ousands): 8 + 2 = 46, so 2 with carryover 8.\n\nMillions place: 7 + 0 + 3 = 1.\n\nTen millions: 7 + 6 = 4.\n\nHundred millions: 0 + 0 = 55, so 8 with carryover 4.\n\nBillions place: the carryover 8.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:.\n\n4 (ones), 6 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 1 (hundred thousands), 5 (millions), 0 (ten millions), 2 (hundred millions), and 6 (billions). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
