 =41. So write down 0 and carry over 4.\n\nBillions place: only the carryover 7. Since both numbers have no digits beyond hundred millions (they are both 7-digit numbers), so the billions place is just 5.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nHundred thousands:9 (with a carryover 7).\n\nMillions:6.\n\nTen millions:5 (with carryover 8).\n\nHundred millions:3 (with carryover 4).\n\nBillions:2. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
