s place:** First number: 0 (since 172,107,958 has 0 in the ten thousands place), second number: 6 (from 614,960,281's ten thousands place is 6). 0 + 6 = 6. No carryover.\n\n**Hundred thousands place:** First number:1, second number:9. 1 +9=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\n**Millions place:** First number:2, second number:4 (since 614,960,281 has 4 in the millions place). 2 +4=6, plus carryover 1 makes 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\n**Ten millions place:** First number:7, second number:1 (from 614 million, so ten millions digit is 1). 7 +1=8. Write 8.\n\n**Hundred millions place:** First number:1, second number:6. 1 +6=7. Write 7.\n\nSo putting it all together from right to left:\n\nUnits:9, tens:3, hundreds:2, thousands:8, ten thousands:6, hundred thousands:0, millions:7, ten millions:8, hundred millions:7.\n\nSo the total is 787,068,239.\n\nWait, that contradicts my previous result. Hmm. Let me check again:\n\nWait, when I broke down the places step by step:\n\nUnits: 8 +1 =9.\n\nTens:5+8=13, so 3 and carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:9+2=11 +1=12 \u21d2 2 and carryover 1.\n\nThousands:7 (from first) +0 (second) =7 +1=8. Carryover 0.\n\nTen thousands:0 +6 =6.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +9=10 \u21d2 0 and carryover 1.\n\nMillions:2 (first) +4 (second) =6 +1=7.\n\nTen millions:7 (first) +1 (second)=8.\n\nHundred millions:1 +6=7.\n\nSo the number is 7 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (units). So the number is 787,068,239.\n\nWait, but in the first method when I thought it was 833 million something, that was incorrect. So which is correct?\n\nAlternatively, let's add them numerically:\n\nFirst number: 172,107,958.\n\nSecond number: 614,960,281.\n\nAdding the two:\n\n172,107,958\n\n+614,960,281\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add 172,107,958 + 600,000,000 = 772,107,958.\n\nThen add the remaining 14,960,281:\n\n772,107,958 + 14,960,281.\n\n772,107,958 + 10,000,000 = 782,107,958.\n\n782,107,958 + 4,960,28