nWait, but let me verify:\n\n963,134,105 + 821,767,453.\n\nLet me compute this using another method.\n\nAdd the millions first:\n\n963,134,105 is 963 million plus 134,105.\n\n821,767,453 is 821 million plus 767,453.\n\nAdding the millions: 963 + 821 = 1,784 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 134,105 + 767,453.\n\n134,105 + 700,000 = 834,105.\n\n834,105 + 67,453 = 901,558.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 1,784,000,000 + 901,558 = 1,784,901,558.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,784,901,558.\n\nWait a second, but when I first tried, I had a different approach but now this method gives a clear result. So I think the confusion earlier was due to misalignment of digits, but this step-by-step addition and breaking into millions makes sense.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 963,134,105 and 821,767,453 is 1,784,901,558.\n</think>\n\nThe sum of 963,134,105 and 821,767,453 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Align the numbers by place value:**\n   \n   ```\n      963,134,105\n    + 821,767,453\n   ---------------\n   ```\n\n2. **Add each column starting from the right (units place):**\n   - **Units:** 5 + 3 = 8\n   - **Tens:** 0 + 5 = 5\n   - **Hundreds:** 1 + 4 = 5\n   - **Thousands:** 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 Write 1, carry over 1\n   - **Ten Thousands:** 3 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 Write 0, carry over 1\n   - **Hundred Thousands:** 1 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 9\n   - **Millions:** 3 + 1 = 4\n   - **Ten Millions:** 6 + 2 = 8\n   - **Hundred Millions:** 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 Write 7, carry over 1\n   - **Billions:** Carry over 1\n\n3. **Combine all digits:**\n   ```\n   1 (Billions) 7 (Hundred Millions) 8 (Ten Millions) 4 (Millions) 9 (Hundred Thousands) 0 (Ten Thousands) 1 (Thousands) 5 (Hundreds) 5 (Tens) 8 (Units)\n   ```\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe sum is **1,784,901,558**.  \n\n\\boxed{1784901558}",
